# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 025
# Act: EVA+  (Evaluation aimed at Figure)   Stance: Binding   Site: Lens
#
# EVA's second use: the witness act itself. Turn-23's claim — "signal, not
# noise," consistent across turn-12 and turn-13 — is tested against
# kernel/data/noise-control.json, a series built by the identical
# construction (same length, same generator family, different seed) with
# NOTHING planted. Checked directly, not assumed: noise-control's value at
# index 16 is -0.46 (an ordinary sample, not null), and its own
# `sign_at_site_role` reads "present" — the general the claim is tested
# against actually holds the opposite value.
#
# This is what makes turn-23's claim witnessed rather than merely
# consistent: consistency (SIG*, DEF*) shows a verdict repeats across
# instances built to carry it. Witnessing (this turn) shows the SAME
# construction, with nothing planted, does NOT produce the verdict. If
# noise-control had also read "absent," turn-23's claim would be exactly
# the vacuous ground eoreader6's SEED.md #3 refuses — a null that would
# clear anything put in front of it, unable to distinguish signal from
# its own construction. It does not, so the claim stands witnessed.
#
# This binds — does not resolve — turn-7's and turn-14's still-distinct
# anchors. EVA is not asked to choose between them here; nothing in this
# kernel has proposed that they compete. What is bound is turn-23's claim
# to independent corroborating evidence, which is EVA's actual job at this
# address per the wiki's own definition: "render judgment... not resolved,
# not reduced, held under evaluation."
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-24 (a candidate and a named
# general). Refuted if noise-control's sign matched "absent" — checked
# above, it reads "present."

:turn-25  eot:opens        :turn-24 .
:turn-25  eot:act          eot:EVA+ .
:turn-25  eot:stance       "Binding" .
:turn-25  eot:site         "Lens" .
:turn-25  eot:tests        :turn-23 .
:turn-25  eot:against      "kernel/data/noise-control.json" .
:turn-25  eot:witnessed    true .
:turn-25  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
